Z||000000||Neverfinished||02-05-2001||03:45 AM||||Since I've been away from my fiero for about 2 months now, I am getting fed up of driving an 86 tercel. I would like to drive it off a cliff since it is the most ugly, gutless rice box on the planet. I shed a small tear (which soon turns to ice) every time I walk past my fiero in the morning. For all you Canadian drivers and all who unfortunatly live with snow; vent your frustrations and list your winter beater and all time worst winter beater.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  ||||reg||6
Z||000001||crzyone||02-05-2001||06:42 AM||||My winter beater is a 85 sport coupe with really good winter tires.  my summer car is an 86 GT fasback so either way I'm happy summer or winter!   plus Fieros are really fun in the snow<P>------------------<BR>86 GT<BR>85 2M4||||reg||1
Z||000002||Voytek||02-05-2001||02:47 PM||||Hey Neverfinished<BR>You from Vernon, B.C.?  I go out there pretty often.  Are you the guy who e-mailed me recently about coming out to Calgary?<BR>My winter beater is an '85 SE V6 auto. so I'm pretty happy too.  I still can't wait till the summer to drive my '87 GT, 5spd.<BR>Voy||||reg||1
Z||000003||fropuff||02-05-2001||04:34 PM||||Mine's a 1980 Oldsmobile Cutlass Supreme LS.  Summer car is a red 86 GT w/ 63K.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000004||TheFiero64||02-05-2001||05:40 PM||||Damn Plymouth Acclaim that is ready to blow up. <B>I hate Chrysler Products</B> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
Z||000005||Fformula88||02-05-2001||05:47 PM||||My current winter ride doesn't really fit into the "beater" category.  Its a 1997 Ford Probe that I have up to 25K miles.  When I bought it my Fiero wasn't running very well so I figured I should get a reliable daily driver.<P>The worst beater I have owned was a 1980 Ford Fairmont wagon I drove for about 3 months in 1995.  It had huge holes in the rear fenders!  One day in November, the exhaust fell off, the blower motor for the defroster went bad and it started running really poorly.  That was the last day I drove it.  I won't complain because I got the car for free, but it was bad!<P>------------------<BR>John<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">      <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2m6<BR>1987 Fiero Sport Coupe *In rebuilding*<BR>1997 Ford Probe SE<BR>AOL IM: Fformula88||||reg||1
Z||000006||2birds||02-05-2001||10:11 PM||||My worst winter beater was a '71 Ranchero that I paid $200 for back in 1985 (senior year).  Olive green metallic, and about a foot of rust all around.  The gas tank fell out on the maiden voyage.  I finally gave up on it and parted it out.<P>My favorite was a 67 VW Type 3 fastback.  The guy that had it before me put headers on it, but forgot the heater boxes.  Had to drive to school with the windows down, scraping the inside all the way, in the Iowa winter. <P>Of course, down here in SE Georgia, I took the sunroof out of my Fiero today...65 degrees and sunshine, while my in-laws have snow.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Neverfinished||02-06-2001||12:50 AM||||Hey Voytek that is me. I'm getting fed up with not driving my car. I drove my fiero one day when it snowed and almost killed myself (bald tires front and rear???????  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ). decided to ratbag my sisters car. I've been driving it since november or start of december and have sucsessfully broke my side mirrors, headlight,turn signal and burnt out two sets of tires (165/80R13's). I don't like winter and I really hate this car. Anyways Voytek, drop me a line or E-mail if you still got em. I should be coming out to edmonton/calagy from the 18th to the 25th of march. I will have my fiero by then and hope to meet your club if you guys meet when i'm down there. <BR>Let me just re-state : winter blows!!!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000008||MontanaFiero||02-06-2001||03:00 AM||||I still drive my '87 coupe, because it's my only runner right now. I found out the hard way that once you get into a spin on ice, you might as well just sit back and enjoy the ride. Guess I will be buying new hub caps this spring. (New snow tires solved my spinning problem)<P>If it ran, I would be driving my '72 GMC 4X4 in the snow.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||fierodave||02-06-2001||04:14 AM||||84 coupe right now<BR>I have had a Fiero the Last three winters in Wi.  <BR>Never got stuck, never put on snow tires,  Never added weight, never ended up in a ditch! (Knock on wood)<P>I just drop the tire pressure to 26 Lbs. in the rear on the 60's in a heavy snow fall! <P>I have gone through snow deep enough to come up on the hood!  :~)<P>FD<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||DavidHenshaw||02-06-2001||01:58 PM||||My winter beater is my wife's 1993 Nissan Sentra SER. Thats the one with the performance package, special suspension and 140 horsepower. I thought the performance was really good until I test drove my 86 GT last summer. Fieros are amazing.<P>Anyway havn't had to park my Fiero more than 2 weeks total this winter. Southern WVa Yes; Fargo No.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
