Z||000015||filthyscarecrow||02-07-2001||01:59 AM||||you guys are gonna hate me. the fiero's been sitting in the garage for about 3 months now. i bought a 94 integra for the winter. added an intake and headers. straight line acceleration is faster in the integra than in the 86SE with the K&N filter and superchip. i think it's just gettin old. the fiero can still spank the integra in the corners, but 3000rpm comes up in the acura and it just screams. and pulls. and keeps on pullin till 7000. i've already outrun guys in eclipse and talon turbos. here's the scary part: it's not even the VTEC version. too bad the engine spins the wrong way, i'd love to drop that into the fiero... <P>but the most fun car i've ever driven: a dodge R/T formula 2000 car. i've never gone that fast before. 1.5g feels funny in the back of my brain... later that day i got into the fiero to drive to the hotel room. it felt like i was driving a 1988 grand marquis...||||reg||4
Z||000016||jerpro||02-07-2001||10:06 AM||||my winter beater is a 84 se soon-to-be-custom as I am getting the dash customized in the spring AND putting a very funny looking wing on it. This is the first winter this car is been driven on, It has been stored all winters since its birth with NO rust. But hey, my 84 will touch the snow before my 87 for sure!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
